{%- assign community_col = collections['community-designs'] -%}
{%- paginate community_col.products by 24 -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Groups come from the collection's shader- tags rather than a hand-kept
  registry (a registry copy here silently dropped scribble-glyph and
  contour-pareidolia designs) or the per-page metafield accumulator that
  replaced it. Tags win on three counts: collection-wide and pre-deduped
  (all_tags), so heading order is stable — alphabetical — across pages and
  re-sorts instead of following whatever the current 24-product slice leads
  with; a Shopify tag cannot contain a comma, so no delimiter can shatter a
  hostile value into phantom groups; and a product the worker created with a
  blank shader still carries its shader-unknown fallback tag, so it renders
  under "unknown" instead of silently nowhere. The worker derives the tag
  and the custom.shader metafield from one normalized slug, so tag-matching
  products groups on the same value the rest of the system filters by.
{%- endcomment -%}

<section class="community-designs-page section-padding">
  <div class="container">
    <h1 class="community-designs-page__heading">Community Designs</h1>
    <p class="community-designs-page__sub">Designs created and shared by the Brightfield community.</p>

    {%- if community_col.products.size == 0 -%}
      <p class="community-designs-page__empty">No designs yet &mdash; be the first to share one!</p>
    {%- else -%}
      <div id="community-page-container">
        {%- for shader_tag in community_col.all_tags -%}
          {%- assign tag_prefix = shader_tag | slice: 0, 7 -%}
          {%- if tag_prefix == 'shader-' -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              all_tags spans the whole collection while products is this
              page's slice, so a tag can have no products here — skip it
              rather than render an empty group.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- assign has_designs = false -%}
            {%- for product in community_col.products -%}
              {%- if product.tags contains shader_tag -%}
                {%- assign has_designs = true -%}
                {%- break -%}
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
            {%- if has_designs -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                The heading's CSS is text-transform: uppercase, so spacing is
                the only transformation the label needs.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- assign shader_label = shader_tag | remove_first: 'shader-' | replace: '-', ' ' -%}
              <div class="community-card-group">
                <h3 class="community-card-group__heading">{{ shader_label | escape }}</h3>
                <div class="product-grid">
                  {%- for product in community_col.products -%}
                    {%- if product.tags contains shader_tag -%}
                      {%- render 'community-card', product: product -%}
                    {%- endif -%}
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </div>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>

      {%- if paginate.pages > 1 -%}
        <nav class="pagination" aria-label="Pagination">{{ paginate | default_pagination }}</nav>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{%- endpaginate -%}

<script src="{{ 'community-designs.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
<script>
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {
    if (window.CommunityDesigns) {
      CommunityDesigns.hydrateInteractions();
    }
  });
</script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Community Designs Page",
  "settings": [],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Community Designs Page" }]
}
{% endschema %}
